assessment.verification_assessment:
Acceptance is observable through a single local fixture, FX-B1P. It starts the composition under systemd `--user`, feeds bounded synthetic events, kills and restarts the process, then checks four things:
(a) identity, order and timestamps are stable across the restart;
(b) already-accepted events survive with no loss or duplication;
(c) each of the five seeded anomaly classes yields a durable anomaly record;
(d) events and anomaly records are readable after restart.
The proof order pins commands and expected outcomes before implementation and requires intact/fault/restored discrimination for the restart control. One independent verifier verdict on the exact candidate SHA is meaningful, because all criteria concern one composition and one fixture. The verdict establishes local capability only and explicitly does not cover WO-220504's operational-target proof.
